:R-HSA-351143  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0097055 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Agmatine is an amine that is formed by decarboxylation of L-arginine by the enzyme arginine decarboxylase (ADC) and hydrolyzed by the enzyme agmatinase to putrescine. Agmatine binds to several target receptors in the brain and has been proposed as a novel neuromodulator (Reghunathan 2006). Agmatine has the potential to serve in the coordination of the early and repair phase pathways of arginine in inflammation (Satriano, 2003)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Agmatine biosynthesis" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Gopinathrao, G, 2008-05-21 17:26:32" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Reviewed: D'Eustachio, P, 2008-06-12 14:43:38" , "Edited: Gopinathrao, G, 2006-04-27 13:13:48" ;
